  "name": "Whales and Walruses as Tillers of the Sea Floor",
  "description": "As gray whales and Pacific walruses gather food from the bottom of the northeastern Bering Sea, they produce pits and furrows to a degree that rivals the disturbances caused by geologic processes. [Reference: Nelson, C.H. and K.R. Johnson. 1987. Whales and Walruses as Tillers of the Sea Floor. Scientific American. 256(2)122-117.]\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To determine the origins of pits and furrows seen in data from side-scan sonography.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23563965",
